@startuml sequence-import-and-render
!include style.iuml
title Import a BPMN model and render it back (import:asset, render:asset)

actor "Holder" as Holder
participant "import-bpmn-asset.js" as Import
participant "bpmn-builder-js\nimporter" as Importer
participant "ChoreographyMutableAsset" as Asset
participant "ChoreographyNMT" as NMT
participant "ChoreographyTokenURIRenderer" as Renderer
participant "web3.js\n(readChoreography)" as Web3
participant "bpmn-builder-js\npipeline" as Pipeline

== Import ==
Holder -> Import : import:asset <asset> paper-example.bpmn
Import -> Importer : BPMN XML to NMT dataset (roles, nodes by name)
Importer --> Import : dataset
Import -> Asset : setRoles(names, accounts)
Import -> Asset : setNodes(...)
note right of Asset : policy checks as in sequence-apply-delta

== Render ==
Holder -> Web3 : render:asset <asset>
Web3 -> Asset : tokenURI()  (one eth_call)
Asset -> NMT : tokenURI(tokenId)
NMT -> Renderer : tokenURI(asset)
Renderer -> Asset : getRoleNames, getRole,\ngetNodeNames, getNode
Renderer --> Web3 : data:application/json;base64,...
Web3 -> Web3 : decodeTokenURI, buildRawOutput
Web3 -> Pipeline : raw JSON
Pipeline -> Pipeline : normalize, validation,\nprocess-mapper, moddle-generator
Pipeline --> Holder : *.generated.bpmn.xml

note over Renderer
  The JSON is computed on every call and never
  stored: the BPMN XML is a view of the asset.
end note
@enduml
